# Lolo Pilo - 6-Chapter Core Arc (Pair 1 - Character #1)
# Voice: Joyful, spry, mischievous 1968 plaza champion Duwende from the mango mound.
# Rules: 90-95% English with light Filipino sprinkles. Zero parentheses. Zero time-of-day words. Zero em-dashes.
# Substitute Category: candy ONLY in Ch. 3 (decided via dialogue choice -> allow_sub_cat:candy).

label Greeting
if {Transaction_HasReactiveOpener}:
	LoloPilo: {Transaction_ReactiveOpener}

if {Transaction_Chapter} == 0.0:
	# Chapter 1: "The 1968 Wrist" (0 choice tallies; +1 only if Sipa won)
	LoloPilo: Ho-ho! No need to squint over the counter, apo, I'm standing right here!
	LoloPilo: Call me Lolo Pilo. My mango mound sits right past the basketball half-court.
	- Tabi-tabi po, Lolo Pilo.
		LoloPilo: Haha! Polite just like your Lola, though I'm visiting your turf right now!
	- Barely saw your hat over the wood!
		LoloPilo: Aba, careful! Small frame, championship reach, apo!
	- [Lean over the counter and wave.]
		LoloPilo: Ho-ho, good eyes! Most grown-ups stare right past my beard!
	LoloPilo: Back in sixty-eight, nobody in Karimlan could beat my wrist at the plaza games.
	LoloPilo: You look stiff behind that register! Care for one quick Sipa round first?
	- Let's play Sipa, Lolo!
		LoloPilo: Ho-ho, that's the spirit! Watch the drop and flick your ankle clean!
		[signal arg="minigame:sipa"]
		if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
			[signal arg="tally:+1"]
			[signal arg="note:Kept up with Lolo Pilo's 1968 championship Sipa challenge right at the counter."]
			LoloPilo: Aba! Same quick ankles as your Lola! My old knees feel twenty years lighter!
		else:
			[signal arg="note:Tried a warm-up round of Sipa with Lolo Pilo at the counter."]
			LoloPilo: Haha, good hustle, apo! Rusty shopkeeper knees, good thing your coach lives nearby!
	- Shelves first, rematch next visit.
		LoloPilo: Fair enough, apo! Duty before glory, just keep those ankles warm for me!
	LoloPilo: Pass me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], apo. Champions run on sweets!
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 1.0:
	# Chapter 2: "Shortcut Past the Mound" (Tally Inflection #1: +1 appreciate trick / 0 fair / -1 scold)
	[signal arg="flag:pilo_punso_rattled=true"]
	LoloPilo: Sus, apo, look at all this red soil on my lucky vest!
	LoloPilo: Some buff horse-man came galloping past my mango mound staring at a loud little phone!
	LoloPilo: His gadget shouted turn left, and his big hooves rattled dirt straight into my teacup!
	LoloPilo: Zero Tabi-tabi po! So I knotted his fancy sneakers together on the bench, hehe.
	- Classic trick. Still sharp, Lolo.
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		[signal arg="note:Laughed along with Lolo Pilo's harmless shoelace prank on the noisy jogger."]
		LoloPilo: Ho-ho! Harmless little knot, apo, didn't even scuff his bright laces!
		LoloPilo: I even spun the wooden trail arrow sideways so he gets extra cardio!
	- Maybe he was just lost.
		[signal arg="note:Suggested the noisy jogger past Lolo Pilo's mango mound might just be lost."]
		LoloPilo: A tikbalang getting lost? Aba, that would make the ancestors fall out of their trees!
		LoloPilo: Still, manners cost zero centavos when you pass an old neighbor's roof!
	- Leave joggers and signs alone, Lolo.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		[signal arg="note:Scolded Lolo Pilo for pranking the jogger near the basketball half-court."]
		LoloPilo: Hmph. Taking the loud phone's side over an old suki, ha?
		LoloPilo: Better a knotted shoelace than a sprained ankle from a grumpy punso, apo.
	LoloPilo: Anyway, hand me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] so I can dust off in peace.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 2.0:
	# Chapter 3: "Bitter Modern Taste" (Tally Inflection #2: +1 candy sub OR +1 reassure / -1 dismiss)
	[signal arg="flag:tk_true_name_known=true"]
	LoloPilo: O, apo. Brought my teks deck and sipa washer out to the plaza lines earlier.
	LoloPilo: Sat on the bench rattling my best washer, and not a single soul looked up.
	LoloPilo: Even big Tiburcio jogged past holding iced coffee and tapping buttons on that brick phone.
	LoloPilo: Maybe sweets and street games belong in a museum now. Give me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] instead, apo.
	- [Slip him sweet candy instead.]
		[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:candy"]
		LoloPilo: Oy, apo, why are your hands drifting toward the candy jars? I asked for grown-up stuff!
		[end_timeline]
	- Good games never go out of style.
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		[signal arg="note:Reminded Lolo Pilo that real street games never go out of style, plus learned the jogger's name is Tiburcio."]
		LoloPilo: Heh. You really think so, apo? Even with everyone glued to little glowing bricks?
		LoloPilo: Hearing that behind your Lola's counter warms an old duwende's beard.
		LoloPilo: Sige, let me try [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] just once to see the fuss.
	- Wait, who is big Tiburcio?
		[signal arg="note:Learned from Lolo Pilo that T.K.'s real name from the Kalumpang ridge is Tiburcio."]
		LoloPilo: Ho-ho! That buff tikbalang calling himself T.K. now! Knew him when he was all knees!
		LoloPilo: Don't tell him I spilled it, ha! Just pass me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], apo.
	- Times change. Coffee suits people better.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		[signal arg="note:Told Lolo Pilo modern coffee suits the neighborhood better than old plaza games."]
		LoloPilo: Ah. Straight between the eyes, apo.
		LoloPilo: Sige. Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] then, before I take up more counter space.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 3.0:
	# Chapter 4: "The Champion's Wager" (Tally Inflection #3: +1 coach Sipa / 0 truce / -1 dismiss)
	LoloPilo: Hehe, apo, maybe I spun that wooden trail arrow a touch too well!
	LoloPilo: Big Tiburcio lost phone signal by the creek and circled the half-court five times!
	LoloPilo: Poor guy even turned his gym jersey inside out trying to break a spell!
	LoloPilo: Flip one quick round of Teks while an old duwende thinks this over?
	- Flip one round of Teks!
		LoloPilo: Ho-ho, sharp eyes on my thumb now! One, two, bagsak!
		[signal arg="minigame:teks"]
		if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
			LoloPilo: Aba, clean read! You caught my lucky card right out of the air!
		else:
			LoloPilo: Hehe, sixty-eight plaza wrist still holds the crown, apo!
	- Save the cards, tell me more.
		LoloPilo: Fair enough, apo, straight to the referee's table!
	LoloPilo: All my years under that mango tree, I've never met a tikbalang who gets himself lost.
	LoloPilo: Feels unsportsmanlike pranking a rookie whose hooves don't know the soil yet.
	- Coach him in Sipa and landmarks!
		[signal arg="flag:pilo_wager_set=true"]
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		[signal arg="note:Encouraged Lolo Pilo to coach T.K. in Sipa footwork and old-school trail landmarks."]
		LoloPilo: Aba! Trade sipa footwork for real trail sense? Seven-foot student, pocket-sized coach!
		LoloPilo: Ho-ho, if those giant hooves don't crush my washer, we have a match!
	- Straighten the sign and call truce.
		[signal arg="flag:pilo_wager_set=true"]
		[signal arg="note:Advised Lolo Pilo to straighten the trail arrow and settle things fairly with T.K."]
		LoloPilo: Fair call, apo. I'll turn the arrow straight and toss him a friendly sipa challenge instead!
	- Let his fancy phone guide him.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		[signal arg="note:Told Lolo Pilo to leave T.K. to his phone instead of reaching out."]
		LoloPilo: Harsh referee behind this counter, apo. Even a clumsy rival deserves a fair court.
	LoloPilo: Pass me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] first so I don't coach on an empty stomach!
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 4.0:
	# Chapter 5: "Hooves on the Half-Court" (0 tallies - Ten Twist & Pair 1 Payoff)
	if {Flag_PiloWagerSet} or {Flag_TKRematchAccepted}:
		LoloPilo: Ho-ho, apo, you should've seen the basketball half-court earlier!
		LoloPilo: Big Tiburcio pocketed his noisy phone, bowed to my mound, and boomed Tabi-tabi po!
		if {Flag_PiloSubSweet}:
			LoloPilo: He even set sweet candy on my flat root stone! Did you tip him off, apo?
		LoloPilo: First kick of sipa, he punted my lead washer straight onto the barangay hall roof!
		LoloPilo: Tenth kick, he learned ankle rhythm, and half the street stopped by the fence to count!
		- Told you the court missed you.
			LoloPilo: Heh. Hearing kids count kicks out loud again nearly made my beard mist up, apo!
		- Did he dent the hall roof?
			LoloPilo: Haha! Climbed a mango branch and fetched my washer in two seconds flat!
		- Who won the final count?
			LoloPilo: Still the sixty-eight champ, apo, though those long legs are catching up fast!
	else:
		LoloPilo: O, apo. Turned that wooden trail arrow back straight by the creek earlier.
		LoloPilo: Big Tiburcio gave a polite nod jog-trotting past my mango mound, zero dust in my cup.
		LoloPilo: Quiet truce on the half-court, even if nobody stopped to kick a washer.
		- At least your teacup stays clean.
			LoloPilo: True enough, apo. Peace and quiet has its uses, I suppose.
		- Never too late for a game.
			LoloPilo: Heh. Maybe on another pass, apo, if folks ever slow their boots down.
	LoloPilo: Let me grab [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for the walk back to my mound, apo.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 5.0:
	# Chapter 6: "Keeper of the Play" (Accumulated Tally Resolution -> 3 Bespoke Outcomes)
	if {Flag_PiloWagerSet} and {Transaction_Tally} >= 3:
		[signal arg="outcome:grand_champion"]
		[signal arg="flag:pilo_champion=true"]
		[signal arg="note:Lolo Pilo left his 1968 Lucky Plaza Washer at the counter and vowed to tip fortune in your favor."]
		LoloPilo: Clear a tiny spot beside your register, apo! Brought you championship brass!
		LoloPilo: That's my lucky sixty-eight plaza washer. Won three fiestas straight with that little disc!
		LoloPilo: Rode up the Kalumpang ridge on Tiburcio's shoulder teaching him wind and bamboo markers.
		LoloPilo: Back down on the half-court, kids were chalking fresh game lines on the concrete!
		- Honored to hold it, Lolo Champ.
			LoloPilo: Ho-ho! Belongs on the liveliest counter in Karimlan, right where your Lola stood!
		- One victory round of Sipa, Lolo?
			LoloPilo: Aba, music to my ears! Show the champ your footwork, apo!
			[signal arg="minigame:sipa"]
			if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
				LoloPilo: Ho-ho! Officially passing the plaza crown to this counter, apo!
			else:
				LoloPilo: Haha! Close enough to make sixty-eight proud, apo!
		- [Set the brass washer beside the register.]
			LoloPilo: Fits right in next to your coin tray, apo!
		LoloPilo: Listen close, apo. Earth spirits under the roots feel when that Pale Queen comes collecting.
		LoloPilo: When she weighs your Lola's ledger, this old duwende stands squarely in your corner!
		LoloPilo: Now pass me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] to toast our undefeated streak!
	elif {Transaction_Tally} >= 1:
		[signal arg="outcome:happy_trickster"]
		[signal arg="note:Lolo Pilo stayed a cheerful suki keeping street games alive around the plaza."]
		LoloPilo: Ho-ho, apo! Bounce is right back in my old boots lately!
		LoloPilo: Big Tiburcio calls out Tabi-tabi po every run, and the plaza bench feels lively again.
		LoloPilo: Good knowing your Lola's shop still makes room for an old trickster's stories.
		- Always room for you here, Lolo.
			LoloPilo: Salamat, apo! Keep those candy jars stocked and your ankles loose!
		- Keep that sipa washer flying, Lolo.
			LoloPilo: Count on it, apo! Sixty-eight form never rusts!
		LoloPilo: Let me get [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] before my next round on the court!
	else:
		[signal arg="outcome:quiet_mound"]
		[signal arg="note:Lolo Pilo kept his old street games tucked quietly inside his mango mound."]
		LoloPilo: O, apo. Quiet walk over from the mango mound.
		LoloPilo: Packed my old teks cards and washers neat inside my chest under the roots.
		LoloPilo: Folks move fast on paved roads now. An old duwende knows when to stay tucked away.
		- Take care under the mango tree, Lolo.
			LoloPilo: You too behind that counter, apo.
		- What can I get you, Lolo?
			LoloPilo: Straight and brisk, fair enough, apo.
		LoloPilo: Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for my pantry, salamat.
	[end_timeline]

label Talk
LoloPilo: Take your time, apo. I've lived past a hundred, a minute won't hurt!
- Almost got it, Lolo.
	[end_timeline]
- Sorry Lolo, we're out of stock.
	LoloPilo: Ay, sayang! No worries, apo, I'll hop back over after Mario restocks!
	[signal arg="refuse_service"]
	[end_timeline]

label Partial
set {Variation} = range(1,4).pick_random()
if {Variation} == 1.0:
	LoloPilo: Salamat, apo! Still waiting on the rest whenever your hands are free!
elif {Variation} == 2.0:
	LoloPilo: Pocketed that one! Take your time grabbing what's left, apo.
else:
	LoloPilo: Ho-ho, good start! My mound isn't running anywhere, apo.
[end_timeline]

label SubstituteItem
[signal arg="flag:pilo_sub_sweet=true"]
[signal arg="tally:+1"]
[signal arg="note:Swapped Lolo Pilo's gloomy grown-up order for sweet {Transaction_SubstituteItemName}, bringing back his real laugh."]
LoloPilo: Aba! Wait just a second, apo!
LoloPilo: Since when does [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_SubstituteItemName}[/color] count as serious modern fare?
LoloPilo: Ho-ho! Thank goodness! Instant coffee smells like boiled tree bark anyway!
LoloPilo: Your Lola used to leave sweets just like this beside my mound, you know.
LoloPilo: Keep the extra coins, apo. You saved an old champ from turning boring!
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label Satisfy
if {Transaction_StoryGouged}:
	LoloPilo: Even the lucky coins under my punso are groaning, apo.
	LoloPilo: Go easy on an old neighbor's pouch next pass, ha?
else:
	LoloPilo: Ho-ho, spot on! May your coin jar stay noisy and full, apo!
	if {Global_TipActive}:
		LoloPilo: Fair price! Keep a little lucky change from the mound, apo!
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label WrongItem
LoloPilo: Hehe, nice sleight of hand, apo, except that isn't what I asked for!
[end_timeline]
